{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>Upon man and beast.</b> And if you say: where did they have beasts from — was it not already stated, ״וַיָּמָת כֹּל מִקְנֵה מִצְרָיִם״? The decree was decreed only upon those in the fields alone, as it is stated, ״בְּמִקְנְךָ אֲשֶׁר בַּשָּׂדֶה״, and one who feared the word of HaShem brought his livestock indoors. So it is taught in the Mekhilta at ״וַיִּקַּח שֵׁשׁ מֵאוֹת רֶכֶב בָּחוּר״ (Exodus 14)."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 9, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:51:12.627516047Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}